==Belarusian==

===Etymology===
Compare to {{cognate|ru|гром}}, {{cognate|uk|грім}}, {{cognate|pl|grom}}, {{cognate|cs|hrom}}, Old Slav [[громъ]]. Originates from Indo-European onomatopoeic ''*ghrem-'': ''*ghrom-''. Compare, for example, with Greek χρεμιζω: χρομος "noise, sound".

